Work Smarter with AI
Pairing with AI has already been shown to significantly boost efficiency and output quality. Research indicates that teams using AI support completed tasks 12.2% more quickly and with a 25.1% increase in speed, yielding results over 40% higher in quality than those without AI1. It's not all about productivity and speed, though - delegating tedious or time-intensive tasks frees up your bandwidth, allowing you to engage in more creative, strategic, and interesting work.

AI's potential applications are virtually limitless, and individuals will develop unique strategies to suit their needs. To begin exploring these possibilities, here are some practical applications and example prompts:

Generate innovative ideas
What [solutions, root causes, strategies, risks, or important considerations] can you think of?
Organize and prioritize ideas and information
Group [this information] into categories.
How should I prioritize these [features, tasks, objectives, or projects] based on [these criteria]?
What patterns, commonalities, or trends exist in this data?
Provide feedback
Give me feedback on this [messaging, plan, idea, or strategy] relating to [criteria].
What else should I consider?
Data collection and analysis interpretation
What data should I collect, and how should I collect it?
What analytical tools best suit this data, and how should I interpret the results?
Enhance collaboration
How should I navigate [problem] with [organization bureaucracy, leadership, or other team members]?
